---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Code from '../../components/Code.astro';
import FlowDiagram from '../../components/FlowDiagram.astro';
import ProfileDiagram from '../../components/ProfileDiagram.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation — Tether CLI"
  description="Install Tether, connect and trust your machines, and manage dotfiles, packages, package security, profiles, and team sync."
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <section id="introduction">
    <p class="eyebrow">YOUR GUIDE TO A CONNECTED ENVIRONMENT</p>
    <h1>Get your machines<br /><em>on the same page.</em></h1>
    <p>
      Tether syncs dotfiles and packages across your machines through Git. It encrypts dotfiles by default and keeps package manifests readable.
    </p>
    <h3>Key Features</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Automatic Sync</strong> — Background daemon syncs changes every 5 minutes</li>
      <li><strong>End-to-End Encryption</strong> — AES-256-GCM encryption with passphrase-protected keys</li>
      <li><strong>Machine Profiles</strong> — Per-machine control over which dotfiles and packages sync</li>
      <li><strong>Project Configs</strong> — Sync .env files and IDE settings across machines by Git remote</li>
      <li><strong>Package Manager Support</strong> — Syncs Homebrew, npm, pnpm, bun, gem, and uv packages</li>
      <li><strong>Supply-Chain Checks</strong> — Synced packages install only from machines you trust, after release-age and OSV checks</li>
      <li><strong>Signed Machine Records</strong> — Each machine signs its package list with its own SSH key</li>
      <li><strong>Secret Detection</strong> — Scans for potential API keys and credentials before syncing</li>
      <li><strong>Git-Backed</strong> — Full version history and rollback capabilities</li>
      <li><strong>Team Secrets</strong> — Share encrypted secrets across teams with age encryption</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-12 border-surface" />

  <!-- Installation -->
  <section id="installation">
    <h2>Installation</h2>
    <h3>Homebrew (macOS and Linux)</h3>
    <Code code={`brew tap paddo-tech/tap
brew install tether-cli`} />
    <h3>Release download (Linux)</h3>
    <p>Download the <code>tether-&lt;version&gt;-&lt;target&gt;.tar.gz</code> file for your CPU (x86_64 or aarch64) from the <a href="https://github.com/paddo-tech/tether-cli/releases">GitHub releases page</a>. Extract it, and put the <code>tether</code> binary in a directory on your <code>PATH</code>.</p>
    <h3>From source</h3>
    <p>You need Rust 1.91 or later.</p>
    <Code code="cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/paddo-tech/tether-cli" />
    <h3>Requirements</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Platform:</strong> macOS or Linux (see <a href="#linux">Linux</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>curl:</strong> Used for OSV malware checks</li>
      <li><strong>Shell:</strong> zsh or bash</li>
      <li><strong>Git:</strong> Configured with GitHub, GitLab, or self-hosted Git server</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-12 border-surface" />

  <!-- Quick Start -->
  <section id="quick-start">
    <h2>Quick Start</h2>
    <p>Connect your first machine, then add the next one.</p>
    <h3>1. Initialize</h3>
    <Code code="tether init" />
    <p>Follow the prompts to configure your Git repository and encryption passphrase.</p>
    <h3>2. Verify Setup</h3>
    <Code code="tether status" />
    <p>You should see the daemon running and your synced files listed.</p>
    <h3>3. On Another Machine</h3>
    <Code code={`brew tap paddo-tech/tap && brew install tether-cli
tether init --repo git@github.com:username/dotfiles.git`} />
    <p>Enter the same passphrase. Your configs sync automatically.</p>
    <h3>4. Trust Your Machines</h3>
    <p>Each machine signs its package list with its own key. Packages from a machine you do not trust wait for approval. On each machine, read its own fingerprint:</p>
    <Code code="tether machines list" />
    <p>On your other machines, trust that machine with the fingerprint you read:</p>
    <Code code="tether machines trust <id> <fingerprint>" />
    <p>See <a href="#machine-trust">Machine Trust</a> for details.</p>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-12 border-surface" />

  <!-- Upgrade -->
  <section id="upgrade">
    <h2>Upgrade to Tether 2.0</h2>
    <p>Tether 2.0 adds signed machine records and checks synced packages before it installs them. After the upgrade, each machine must trust your other machines once. Until then, packages from those machines wait for approval.</p>
    <p>You can upgrade one machine at a time. Machines on 1.13.1 keep working with the same repo during the upgrade.</p>

    <h3>1. Upgrade a machine</h3>
    <Code code="brew upgrade tether-cli" />
    <p>If you installed a release download or built from source, install the new version the same way. See <a href="#installation">Installation</a>.</p>

    <h3>2. Sync it once</h3>
    <Code code="tether sync" />
    <p>The first sync makes the machine's signing key and signs its record.</p>

    <h3>3. Trust your upgraded machines</h3>
    <p>On each upgraded machine, run <code>tether machines list</code>. Note the fingerprint in the row marked "(this machine)". Then, on your other upgraded machines, trust it:</p>
    <Code code="tether machines trust <id> <fingerprint>" />
    <p>You can also approve the "trust machine" item when <code>tether sync</code> asks, or on the dashboard Security tab.</p>
    <p>A machine that still runs 1.13.1 has no signed record. Its packages wait in the inbox as "from another machine". Upgrade that machine, sync it, and trust it. The next sync then installs its packages.</p>

    <h3>4. Review held packages</h3>
    <Code code="tether packages inbox" />
    <p>After you trust a machine, the next sync installs the packages its record lists. Packages that fail a check stay in the inbox.</p>

    <h3>5. Check your settings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Add third-party Homebrew taps that you use to <code>packages.brew.trusted_taps</code></li>
      <li>Add packages that need install scripts to <code>packages.allow_scripts</code></li>
      <li>Change <code>packages.min_release_age_days</code> if 7 days does not suit you</li>
      <li>Remove records that <code>tether machines list</code> marks as an old id of this machine</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What changed</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Synced packages no longer install on their own unless a trusted machine record lists that exact version</li>
      <li>Packages from untrusted Homebrew taps now wait in the inbox. Before, Tether skipped them with a warning</li>
      <li>Packages for managers that cannot enforce the release-age limit now wait in the inbox. This covers gem and older npm, pnpm and bun</li>
      <li>Tether no longer runs <code>brew update</code>. Run it yourself to update Homebrew</li>
      <li><code>tether machines rename</code> renames only the machine it runs on</li>
      <li>The Config tab no longer shows the <code>sync_versions</code> settings. Tether still writes them as <code>false</code>, because 1.x builds need them to read the synced config</li>
      <li>The dashboard shows a machine as online when its record is at most 90 minutes old</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-12 border-surface" />

  <!-- Linux -->
  <section id="linux">
    <h2>Linux</h2>
    <p>Tether runs on x86_64 and aarch64 Linux. Install it with Homebrew, a release download, or from source. See <a href="#installation">Installation</a>. Then run <code>tether init</code>.</p>

    <h3>Daemon</h3>
    <Code code="tether daemon install" />
    <p>On Linux, this installs and enables a systemd user service in <code>~/.config/systemd/user/tether.service</code>. The service gets your shell's <code>PATH</code>, <code>GEM_HOME</code>, and <code>GEM_PATH</code>. <code>tether daemon uninstall</code> removes it.</p>
    <p>Without a systemd user session, use <code>tether daemon start</code>.</p>
    <p>Paths with spaces, <code>$</code>, or <code>%</code> work. systemd cannot run a program whose path has a quote, a backslash, or a control character. In that case, <code>tether daemon install</code> stops with an error and writes no unit.</p>

    <h3>Notifications</h3>
    <p>Tether uses <code>notify-send</code> for desktop notifications. Without it, Tether logs this once and shows no notifications.</p>

    <h3>Packages</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Tether does not install Homebrew casks on Linux</li>
      <li>Tether skips gems that ship with Ruby or with Debian. On a Ruby from ruby-build or rbenv, Tether cannot identify these gems</li>
      <li>Machine records name their OS. When only Macs list a version, Linux tries it first. If it fails, Tether holds the newest release that suits Linux in the inbox as "another OS pins a version that fails here". Approve it to install exactly that release</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Merge tool</h3>
    <p>When the synced merge tool is <code>opendiff</code>, a machine without it uses <code>vimdiff</code>. To use another tool on one machine, set it in <a href="#local-config"><code>~/.tether/local.toml</code></a>.</p>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-12 border-surface" />

  <!-- How It Works -->
  <section id="how-it-works">
    <h2>How It Works</h2>
    <h3>Architecture</h3>
    <p>
      Tether uses your Git repository to connect machines. The daemon detects changes and encrypts dotfiles before pushing them to Git.
    </p>
    <p>
      On your other machines, Tether pulls these changes and applies them automatically.
    </p>
    <h3>Sync Flow</h3>
    <FlowDiagram label="FROM YOUR MACHINE TO YOUR REPO" caption="Other machines pull these changes, decrypt the dotfiles, and apply them locally." steps={[
      { icon: 'file', title: 'Scan changes', detail: 'Check files and package manifests' },
      { icon: 'lock', title: 'Encrypt dotfiles', detail: 'Use your local encryption key' },
      { icon: 'git', title: 'Sync through Git', detail: 'Commit and push to your repo' },
    ]} />
    <ol>
      <li>Daemon detects file changes (every 5 minutes or manual <code>tether sync</code>)</li>
      <li>Secret scanner checks for credentials</li>
      <li>Files are encrypted (if enabled)</li>
      <li>Tether signs this machine's record of its packages</li>
      <li>Changes committed and pushed to Git</li>
      <li>Other machines pull and decrypt</li>
      <li>Other machines verify the record and check each new package before they install it</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>Data Layout</h3>
    <p>Local Tether data lives in <code>~/.tether/</code>:</p>
    <Code code={`~/.tether/
├── config.toml      # Configuration (versioned)
├── local.toml       # Settings for this machine only (never synced)
├── state.json       # Sync state (hashes, timestamps)
├── sync/            # Personal sync repo
├── teams/<name>/    # Team sync repos
├── collabs/         # Collab project configs
├── backups/         # File backups
├── identity.pub     # Age public key (for team secrets)
├── signing_key      # This machine's SSH signing key
├── trusted_keys     # Machine keys this machine trusts (never synced)
├── record_generations.json  # Newest record accepted per key (never synced)
├── machine.json     # This machine's last record (never synced)
├── inbox.json       # Approval inbox (never synced)
├── run/             # Empty working directory for package managers
├── daemon.pid       # Daemon process ID
├── daemon.log       # Daemon logs
└── conflicts.json   # Conflict state`} />
    <p>The sync repository structure:</p>
    <Code code={`sync/
├── profiles/<name>/ # Profile-specific dotfiles (encrypted)
├── dotfiles/        # Flat-layout dotfiles (legacy/shared)
├── configs/         # App configs (tether config, etc.)
├── projects/        # Project-local configs
├── manifests/       # Package manifests
└── machines/        # Per-machine records (<id>.json) and signatures (<id>.json.sig)`} />
  </section>

  <hr class="my-12 border-surface" />

  <!-- Dashboard -->
  <section id="dashboard">
    <h2>Dashboard (TUI)</h2>
    <p>
      Run <code>tether</code> with no arguments to launch the interactive terminal dashboard.
    </p>
    <Code code="tether" />
    <p>The dashboard has six tabs. Switch tabs with the number keys, <code>Tab</code>, or a mouse click.</p>

    <h3>Tabs</h3>
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface">
          <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Tab</th>
          <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Key</th>
          <th class="text-left py-2">Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Overview</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">1</td>
          <td class="py-2">Dotfiles, packages, machines, recent activity, and a chart of sync commits per day</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Files</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">2</td>
          <td class="py-2">Browse synced dotfiles with file history, diffs with line numbers, and restore</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Packages</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">3</td>
          <td class="py-2">Collapsible package manager sections, manifest history, failed installs, and uninstall with confirmation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Machines</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">4</td>
          <td class="py-2">A card for each machine: id, profile, OS, Tether version, packages, last sync, online/idle/stale state, and key trust</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Config</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">5</td>
          <td class="py-2">Inline config editor with toggles, validated text fields, list editing, and the package security settings</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Security</td>
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">6</td>
          <td class="py-2">The approval inbox: held packages with their reasons, source machine, commit, and OSV advisories, machine keys that wait for trust, and the trusted machines</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>A machine is online when its record is at most 90 minutes old. An idle machine updates its record once an hour. After 24 hours without an update, the card shows the machine as stale.</p>

    <h3>Themes</h3>
    <p>On a terminal with true color, the dashboard uses Catppuccin Mocha or Latte. It picks one from the terminal background. Other terminals get a 16-color theme. To choose a theme, set <code>dashboard.theme</code>:</p>
    <Code code="tether config set dashboard.theme mocha   # mocha, latte, ansi, or auto" />

    <h3>Keybindings</h3>
    <p>You can also click a tab, a row, or a key hint, and scroll lists with the mouse wheel.</p>
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface">
          <th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Key</th>
          <th class="text-left py-2">Action</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Ctrl+K</td>
          <td class="py-2">Search actions, tabs, files, and packages</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">s</td>
          <td class="py-2">Trigger a manual sync</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">d</td>
          <td class="py-2">Toggle daemon start/stop</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">r</td>
          <td class="py-2">Refresh dashboard data</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">?</td>
          <td class="py-2">Show help overlay with all keybindings</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">1-6</td>
          <td class="py-2">Switch to tab by number</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Tab</td>
          <td class="py-2">Next tab</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">↑ ↓ / j k</td>
          <td class="py-2">Navigate within lists (on the Machines tab, also ← → / h l)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">Enter</td>
          <td class="py-2">Expand/collapse sections, confirm actions</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">h</td>
          <td class="py-2">Show manifest history (Packages tab)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">p</td>
          <td class="py-2">Open profile picker (Machines tab)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">D</td>
          <td class="py-2">Remove a record that may be an old id of this machine (Machines tab)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">a</td>
          <td class="py-2">Approve and install a package, or trust a machine key (Security tab)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">x</td>
          <td class="py-2">Reject a package, tap, or key (Security tab)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">A</td>
          <td class="py-2">Approve all packages that are not malicious (Security tab)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-surface/50">
          <td class="py-2 pr-4 font-mono text-xs">q / Esc / Ctrl+c</td>
          <td class="py-2">Quit dashboard</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Approval questions and the old-record removal question ignore keys for 0.4 seconds after they open. Thus a key that you typed for another screen cannot answer them. Enter cancels them.</p>
  </section>

  <hr class="my-12 border-surface" />

  <!-- Commands -->
  <section id="commands">
    <h2>Commands</h2>

    <h3 id="cmd-dashboard">tether / tether dashboard</h3>
    <p>Launch the interactive TUI dashboard. See <a href="#dashboard">Dashboard</a> above for details.</p>
    <Code code="tether" />

    <h3 id="cmd-init">tether init</h3>
    <p>Initialize Tether on this machine.</p>
    <Code code="tether init [--repo <URL>] [--no-daemon]" />
    <ul>
      <li><code>--repo &lt;URL&gt;</code> — Git repository URL (interactive if omitted)</li>
      <li><code>--no-daemon</code> — Don't start daemon after init</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-sync">tether sync</h3>
    <p>Manually trigger a sync.</p>
    <Code code="tether sync [--dry-run] [--force]" />
    <ul>
      <li><code>--dry-run</code> — Show what would be synced</li>
      <li><code>--force</code> — Skip conflict prompts</li>
    </ul>
    <p>In a terminal, <code>tether sync</code> asks about packages and machine keys that wait for approval. The daemon holds them and sends one notification for each new batch.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-status">tether status</h3>
    <p>Show current sync status, daemon state, and synced files.</p>
    <Code code="tether status" />

    <h3 id="cmd-diff">tether diff</h3>
    <p>Show differences between machines.</p>
    <Code code="tether diff [--machine <NAME>]" />
    <ul>
      <li><code>--machine &lt;NAME&gt;</code> — Compare with specific machine</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-daemon">tether daemon</h3>
    <p>Control the background daemon.</p>
    <Code code="tether daemon <start|stop|restart|logs|install|uninstall>" />
    <ul>
      <li><code>start</code> — Start the daemon</li>
      <li><code>stop</code> — Stop the daemon</li>
      <li><code>restart</code> — Restart the daemon</li>
      <li><code>logs</code> — View last 50 log lines</li>
      <li><code>install</code> — Install the login service: launchd on macOS, a systemd user service on Linux</li>
      <li><code>uninstall</code> — Remove the login service</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-machines">tether machines</h3>
    <p>Manage machines, machine trust, and profiles in the sync network.</p>
    <Code code="tether machines <list|rename|remove|trust|untrust|profile>" />
    <ul>
      <li><code>list</code> — List all machines with profile, version, last sync, key fingerprint, and trust state. It also marks records that may be an old id of this machine</li>
      <li><code>rename &lt;OLD&gt; &lt;NEW&gt;</code> — Rename this machine. Tether signs its record again under the new id. Other machines must trust the new id</li>
      <li><code>remove &lt;NAME&gt;</code> — Remove a machine record and its trusted key on this machine. With <code>-y</code>, Tether removes it without a question</li>
      <li><code>trust &lt;NAME&gt; [FINGERPRINT]</code> — Trust a machine's signing key if its fingerprint matches. Without a fingerprint, Tether shows the current one and asks</li>
      <li><code>untrust &lt;NAME&gt;</code> — Stop trusting a machine's signing key</li>
      <li><code>profile set &lt;PROFILE&gt;</code> — Assign a profile to this machine</li>
      <li><code>profile unset</code> — Remove profile assignment</li>
      <li><code>profile create &lt;NAME&gt;</code> — Create a new profile</li>
      <li><code>profile edit &lt;NAME&gt;</code> — Edit profile dotfile/package config</li>
      <li><code>profile list</code> — List all profiles and assignments</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-ignore">tether ignore</h3>
    <p>Manage ignore patterns and per-machine exclusions.</p>
    <Code code={`# Secret scanning patterns
tether ignore add <PATTERN>
tether ignore list
tether ignore remove <PATTERN>

# Per-machine file exclusions
tether ignore dotfile <FILE>
tether ignore project <PROJECT> <PATH>
tether ignore sync-list
tether ignore sync-remove <FILE>`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-config">tether config</h3>
    <p>Manage configuration.</p>
    <Code code={`tether config get <KEY>
tether config set <KEY> <VALUE>
tether config edit
tether config dotfiles
tether config features              # List feature toggles
tether config features enable <F>   # Enable a feature
tether config features disable <F>  # Disable a feature`} />
    <ul>
      <li><code>get &lt;KEY&gt;</code> — Get config value (supports nested keys like <code>packages.brew.enabled</code>)</li>
      <li><code>set &lt;KEY&gt; &lt;VALUE&gt;</code> — Set config value</li>
      <li><code>edit</code> — Open config in editor</li>
      <li><code>dotfiles</code> — Interactive UI for managing synced files</li>
      <li><code>features</code> — Manage feature toggles (see <a href="#feature-toggles">Feature Toggles</a>)</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-team">tether team</h3>
    <p>Manage team sync repositories, secrets, and project sharing.</p>
    <Code code={`# Team management
tether team setup                     # Interactive wizard
tether team add <URL>                 # Add team repo
tether team list                      # List teams
tether team status                    # Show status
tether team enable/disable            # Toggle sync

# Organization mapping
tether team orgs add <ORG>            # Map GitHub org to team
tether team orgs list                 # List mapped orgs
tether team orgs remove <ORG>         # Unmap org

# Team secrets (age encryption)
tether team secrets add-recipient <KEY>   # Add member's public key
tether team secrets list-recipients       # List recipients
tether team secrets set <NAME>            # Set a secret
tether team secrets get <NAME>            # Get a secret
tether team secrets list                  # List all secrets

# Project secrets
tether team projects add <FILE>       # Share project secret
tether team projects list             # List shared secrets
tether team projects migrate          # Auto-migrate to team
tether team projects purge-personal   # Remove personal copies`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-resolve">tether resolve</h3>
    <p>Resolve file conflicts.</p>
    <Code code="tether resolve [FILE]" />
    <p>Interactive resolution: keep local, use remote, merge, or skip.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-unlock">tether unlock</h3>
    <p>Unlock encryption key with passphrase.</p>
    <Code code="tether unlock" />

    <h3 id="cmd-lock">tether lock</h3>
    <p>Clear cached encryption key.</p>
    <Code code="tether lock" />

    <h3 id="cmd-upgrade">tether upgrade</h3>
    <p>Upgrade all installed packages across enabled package managers.</p>
    <Code code="tether upgrade" />
    <ul>
      <li>npm, pnpm, bun and uv upgrades skip releases newer than <code>packages.min_release_age_days</code></li>
      <li>Tether checks each npm, pnpm, bun, uv and gem upgrade target against OSV. A target with a <code>MAL-</code> advisory waits in the inbox, and the installed version stays</li>
      <li>Tether asks before it upgrades a manager that cannot enforce the release-age limit. Without a terminal, it skips that manager</li>
      <li>Homebrew upgrades include only outdated packages from trusted taps. Tether does not run <code>brew update</code>. Run it yourself to update Homebrew</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-history">tether history</h3>
    <p>Show the change history of a dotfile from the sync repo.</p>
    <Code code="tether history <FILE> [--limit <N>]" />

    <h3 id="cmd-restore">tether restore</h3>
    <p>Restore files from backup or git history.</p>
    <Code code={`tether restore list              # List available backups
tether restore file              # Interactive restore
tether restore file --from <TS>  # Restore from specific timestamp
tether restore git <FILE>        # Restore a dotfile from git history`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-rollback">tether rollback</h3>
    <p>Roll back a package manager's installed packages to a manifest commit.</p>
    <Code code="tether rollback packages <MANAGER> <COMMIT>" />
    <p>Tether lists each package and version it would install, and asks before it changes anything. Without a terminal, it needs <code>-y</code>. A snapshot version other than the newest trusted version installs only when you confirm it in a terminal. <code>-y</code> does not confirm it. Packages that fail a check wait in the inbox.</p>

    <h3 id="cmd-identity">tether identity</h3>
    <p>Manage age identity for team secrets encryption.</p>
    <Code code={`tether identity init     # Generate new age identity
tether identity show     # Show your public key
tether identity unlock   # Unlock with passphrase
tether identity lock     # Clear cached key
tether identity reset    # Generate new (destroys old)`} />

    <h3 id="cmd-packages">tether packages</h3>
    <p>List installed packages across all managers with interactive multi-select uninstall. Review the approval inbox.</p>
    <Code code={`tether packages                          # Interactive mode
tether packages --list                   # Non-interactive list
tether packages inbox                    # List held packages, taps, and keys
tether packages approve <ID> [EXPECTED]  # Approve and install, or trust a key
tether packages reject <ID> [EXPECTED]   # Stop offering that version, tap, or key`} />
    <ul>
      <li><code>--list</code> — Print packages and failed installs without interactive UI</li>
      <li><code>-y</code> — Skip confirmation prompts</li>
      <li><code>&lt;ID&gt;</code> — The item id from <code>inbox</code>, such as <code>npm:typescript</code> or <code>machine:work-laptop</code></li>
      <li><code>[EXPECTED]</code> — The version, Homebrew tap, or key fingerprint you reviewed. It is required without a terminal. Tether refuses the decision when the item changed</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 id="cmd-collab">tether collab</h3>
    <p>Share project secrets with GitHub collaborators (requires write access).</p>
    <Code code={`tether collab init              # Initialize collab for current project
tether collab join <URL>        # Join existing collab
tether collab add <FILE>        # Add secret file (e.g., .env)
tether collab refresh           # Re-encrypt for current collaborators
tether collab list              # List all collabs
tether collab remove            # Remove a collab`} />
  </section>

